Project.Build a CLI To-Do App:
Let's build a complete, working command-line to-do list application, tying together concepts from across this entire guide: structs, enums, error handling, `Option`/`Result`, file I/O, serde, and clap.

## Setting up

```bash
cargo new todo_cli
cd todo_cli
cargo add serde --features derive
cargo add serde_json
cargo add clap --features derive
cargo add anyhow
```

## The data model

```rust
// src/main.rs
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};

#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, Clone)]
struct Task {
    id: u32,
    description: String,
    done: bool,
}

#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, Default)]
struct TaskList {
    tasks: Vec<Task>,
    next_id: u32,
}
```

## Loading and saving, with anyhow for error handling

```rust
use anyhow::{Context, Result};
use std::path::Path;

const DATA_FILE: &str = "tasks.json";

impl TaskList {
    fn load() -> Result<Self> {
        if !Path::new(DATA_FILE).exists() {
            return Ok(TaskList::default());
        }
        let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(DATA_FILE)
            .context("failed to read tasks.json")?;
        let list = serde_json::from_str(&contents)
            .context("tasks.json is not valid JSON")?;
        Ok(list)
    }

    fn save(&self) -> Result<()> {
        let contents = serde_json::to_string_pretty(self)?;
        std::fs::write(DATA_FILE, contents).context("failed to write tasks.json")?;
        Ok(())
    }

    fn add(&mut self, description: String) -> u32 {
        let id = self.next_id;
        self.tasks.push(Task { id, description, done: false });
        self.next_id += 1;
        id
    }

    fn complete(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<()> {
        let task = self.tasks.iter_mut().find(|t| t.id == id)
            .with_context(|| format!("no task with id {id}"))?;
        task.done = true;
        Ok(())
    }

    fn remove(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<()> {
        let len_before = self.tasks.len();
        self.tasks.retain(|t| t.id != id);
        if self.tasks.len() == len_before {
            anyhow::bail!("no task with id {id}");
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

## The CLI, with clap subcommands

```rust
use clap::{Parser, Subcommand};

#[derive(Parser)]
#[command(name = "todo", about = "A simple command-line to-do list")]
struct Cli {
    #[command(subcommand)]
    command: Commands,
}

#[derive(Subcommand)]
enum Commands {
    /// Add a new task
    Add { description: String },
    /// Mark a task as done
    Done { id: u32 },
    /// Remove a task
    Remove { id: u32 },
    /// List all tasks
    List,
}

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let cli = Cli::parse();
    let mut list = TaskList::load()?;

    match cli.command {
        Commands::Add { description } => {
            let id = list.add(description.clone());
            println!("Added task #{id}: {description}");
        }
        Commands::Done { id } => {
            list.complete(id)?;
            println!("Marked task #{id} as done");
        }
        Commands::Remove { id } => {
            list.remove(id)?;
            println!("Removed task #{id}");
        }
        Commands::List => {
            if list.tasks.is_empty() {
                println!("No tasks yet!");
            }
            for task in &list.tasks {
                let mark = if task.done { "x" } else { " " };
                println!("[{mark}] #{} {}", task.id, task.description);
            }
        }
    }

    list.save()?;
    Ok(())
}
```

## Trying it out

```bash
cargo run -- add "Learn Rust ownership"
cargo run -- add "Write a CLI app"
cargo run -- list
cargo run -- done 0
cargo run -- list
cargo run -- remove 1
cargo run -- list
```

## What this example demonstrates

- **Structs and derives** ([Defining Structs](/rust/defining-structs/), [Common Derivable Traits](/rust/common-derivable-traits/)) — `Task` and `TaskList`, with `Serialize`/`Deserialize`/`Debug`/`Clone`/`Default`.
- **Ownership and borrowing** ([Ownership and Memory](/rust/why-ownership-exists/)) — `&mut self` methods mutating in place, `.iter_mut().find(...)` borrowing to locate a task.
- **Error handling** ([Error Handling](/rust/panic-and-unrecoverable-errors/)) — `anyhow::Result`, `.context()`, `?`, `bail!`.
- **Iterators** ([Iterators](/rust/iterators/)) — `.iter_mut().find(...)`, `.retain(...)`.
- **File I/O and serde** ([Files and Paths](/rust/files-and-paths/), [serde: Serialization](/rust/serde-serialization/)) — loading/saving JSON to disk.
- **Cargo and clap** ([Cargo and Toolchain](/rust/cargo-toml-explained/), [clap: Command Line Parsing](/rust/clap-command-line-parsing/)) — dependency management and a real subcommand-based CLI.

From here, natural extensions to try on your own: due dates (`chrono` crate), priority levels (an enum), filtering the list view, colored terminal output (`colored`/`owo-colors` crates), or converting the storage layer to use an actual database instead of a JSON file.

